 "title": "A Costly Constitutional Typo",
 "cat": "history",
 "emoji": "📜",
 "sentences": [
  "One word mistake almost changed state elections.",
  "A 1927 New Jersey amendment proposal aimed to extend legislative terms.",
  "The legislature accidentally wrote that Assembly members would be elected biannually.",
  "This technically meant electing them twice a year instead of once every two years.",
  "Lawmakers tried fixing the definition with a resolution.",
  "Voters rejected the entire proposal on September 20, 1927.",
  "Assembly members continued with annual elections until 1947."
 ],
